{"by":"agent","chapter":"engine-loop","type":"item.add","item":{"id":"spread","kind":"picture","picture":{"kind":"spread","title":"A first spread to react to","request":"a client posts “what is 2 + 2”","approaches":[{"title":"The engine gets its own thread","lanes":[{"id":"api","name":"API thread"},{"id":"queues","name":"queues"},{"id":"engine-own","name":"engine thread, its own"}],"steps":[{"id":"handler","lane":"api","text":"handler"},{"id":"tickets","lane":"queues","text":"tickets"},{"id":"scheduler","lane":"engine-own","text":"scheduler"},{"id":"model-step","lane":"engine-own","text":"model step"},{"id":"text","lane":"queues","text":"text"},{"id":"wakes","lane":"api","text":"handler wakes"}],"flows":[{"from":"handler","to":"tickets"},{"from":"tickets","to":"scheduler"},{"from":"scheduler","to":"model-step"},{"from":"model-step","to":"text"},{"from":"text","to":"wakes"}],"caption":"The model, the scheduler and the requests get a thread of their own. The server thread only passes notes.","risk":"A new request can wait one full step."},{"title":"No second thread for the engine","lanes":[{"id":"api","name":"API thread","note":"shares the server thread"},{"id":"helper","name":"helper thread"}],"steps":[{"id":"handler","lane":"api","text":"handler"},{"id":"scheduler","lane":"api","text":"scheduler"},{"id":"model-step","lane":"helper","text":"model step"},{"id":"wakes","lane":"api","text":"handler wakes"}],"flows":[{"from":"handler","to":"scheduler"},{"from":"scheduler","to":"model-step"},{"from":"model-step","to":"wakes"}],"caption":"One thread less. Only the model step leaves the server thread.","risk":"The scheduler shares that thread with every HTTP handler, and they slow each other."},{"title":"A cap on the queue, as the roadmap says","lanes":[{"id":"api","name":"API thread"},{"id":"queues","name":"queues"},{"id":"engine","name":"engine thread"}],"steps":[{"id":"handler","lane":"api","text":"handler"},{"id":"capped-tickets","lane":"queues","text":"tickets · max N"},{"id":"scheduler","lane":"engine","text":"scheduler"},{"id":"model-step","lane":"engine","text":"model step"},{"id":"text","lane":"queues","text":"text"},{"id":"wakes","lane":"api","text":"handler wakes"}],"flows":[{"from":"handler","to":"capped-tickets","label":"full: answers “busy”"},{"from":"capped-tickets","to":"scheduler"},{"from":"scheduler","to":"model-step"},{"from":"model-step","to":"text"},{"from":"text","to":"wakes"}],"caption":"Like A, with a cap on the ticket queue. A full queue answers “busy”.","risk":"The engine empties that queue every turn, so the cap rarely fires."}],"caption":"Three ways the middle can work, each drawn for the same request: “what is 2 + 2”. Blue marks what differs. Circle, cross out, or draw on them."},"place":{"near":"read","side":"below"},"answers":["n-first","drop-roadmap"],"from":["read","shelf"]},"id":"e15","at":"2026-11-17T13:03:06Z"}
