{"by":"agent","chapter":"engine-loop","type":"item.add","item":{"id":"focus","kind":"picture","picture":{"kind":"focus","lane":"bridge","title":"The bridge, opened","summary":"Down. Tickets are plain data. The queue itself has no cap, because the door already counts every open request. Up. The engine never waits for a handler. It hands this turn’s bundle to the server thread and goes on.","crosses":[{"dir":"in","what":"Submit","part":"engine-client","note":"a new request"},{"dir":"in","what":"Abort","part":"engine-client","note":"the client left"},{"dir":"in","what":"Shutdown","part":"engine-client","note":"stop everything"},{"dir":"out","what":"Delta","part":"stream","note":"a piece of text"},{"dir":"out","what":"Finished","part":"stream","note":"the end, with counts"},{"dir":"out","what":"Failed","part":"stream","note":"the end, with a reason"}],"inside":[{"name":"EngineClient, the door","plain":"61 of 64 open"},{"name":"Inbound queue","plain":"a ticket waits at most one step","holds":["Submit req-44","Abort req-41","Submit req-43"]},{"name":"Engine loop","plain":"takes every ticket at the start of a turn"},{"name":"Output queues","plain":"one for each open request","holds":["req-41 “The”","req-42 “2”","req-43 “Hi”"]},{"name":"This turn’s outputs","plain":"one bundle: “The”, “2”, “Hi”"},{"name":"One wake-up per turn","plain":"not one per token"}],"promise":"Every accepted request gets exactly one ending, and nothing after it. No request can wait forever, even if the engine dies.","cost":"A new request can wait one full step before the engine sees it. A long prefill makes that wait longer.","made":{"title":"One wake-up for each engine turn, not one for each token.","body":"The server thread wakes less often."},"options":{"title":"Two ways to stop a flood","items":[{"id":"cap-queue","name":"Cap the ticket queue","body":"The roadmap’s way: the ticket queue, cap 8, emptied every turn. The waiting line inside the engine has no cap.","risk":"The cap sits where nothing piles up. The line behind it keeps growing."},{"id":"cap-door","name":"Cap the door","body":"Count the open requests. The door counts everything the engine still holds: 3 in the queue, 40 waiting, 1 running, 20 leaving = 64. The 65th hears “busy, come back in 1 s” at once."}],"lean":"cap-door"},"lean":"Cap the door. It needs no shared counter, and a client that leaves can always be told. It changes one sentence in the roadmap."},"place":{"near":"pipe","side":"below"},"answers":["e42","note-fills"],"from":["pipe"]},"id":"e43","at":"2026-11-17T13:09:43Z"}
